    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T22:27:25Z",
    "body": "Claim released. The fixture fix exposes a program-level gouge finding that needs geometry or simulation investigation. I raised effort:high to effort:max under the work-issue escalation rule. I did not weaken the no-gouge assertion.\n\nOn upstream/main 17a8c6e7, I added an assertion that gate.skipped is absent. The unchanged fixture failed that assertion in the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_1_of_6_has_no_gouge. R1 was never generated.\n\nI then removed R1 and its unused tool from sample_job. Verification ran with no skipped or not_judged field. The existing no-gouge assertion failed: \"gouge: program cuts below the model in 150 cell(s), worst 12.69 mm at (0.09, -1.38, z 73.16)\". The reply also had held_by=[\"S1\"] and 274 findings. This does not yet establish whether the gouge report or the generated path is wrong. The shank/holder collision investigation remains unfinished.\n\nCommand: cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test shared_face_bodies_finish the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_1_of_6_has_no_gouge -- --ignored --exact. Both test runs reached their assertions. I unset RUSTC_WRAPPER only in the command's shell because the inherited sccache daemon could not write its configured cache directory.\n\nHeld local work: branch issue/1840-finish-verify-gate in /Users/mikekinney/CamcraftPool/.claude/worktrees/issue-1840. The uncommitted patch is also at /tmp/1840-held.patch. Failure logs are /tmp/1840-red.log and /tmp/1840-after.log. Nothing was committed or pushed. No PR was opened. Mutation checks, other bands, quick gate and clippy were not run because the minimal fixture fix failed its pin. The issue is free for the next worker.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
